# Line endings are checked in as LF and stay LF.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the Windows default and it rewrites the working copy on
# checkout. For most files that is merely noisy; for the shell scripts here it is
# fatal — `gradlew`, `gw.sh` and `tools/*.sh` will not run on Linux or macOS with
# CRLF line endings, and the error ("bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M") does not name
# the cause. `-text` tells git to leave every file exactly as committed, so the
# working copy, the blob and what a cloner gets are the same bytes.
* -text

# Language stats: the ledgers and design docs are prose about the app, not the
# app. Without this GitHub would call a Kotlin project "Markdown".
*.md linguist-documentation
docs/** linguist-documentation
